    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d309">

                <pb facs="0263" n="191" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg191"/>

                <head>Merchants, Brokers, and others of Cardiff</head>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Edward Burch</hi>, <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul for the United States of America at Cardiff:</hi>
                </p>
                <p>We, the undersigned, the merchants, brokers, and others at this port, beg to
                    convey to you our sympathy, indignation, and horror at the assassination of Mr.
                    Lincoln, the President of the United States. We feel that his loss will be
                    deplored not only by the British nation, but throughout the civilized world, and
                    we sincerely trust and believe that the great nation you represent will be able
                    to bear with dignity, and that its future progress will in no way be impeded by,
                    the great and irreparable loss it has sustained.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">Dated this <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1865-04-29">29th day of April, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>JOHN PRIDE, <hi rendition="#italic">Mayor</hi>.</item>
                            <item>WILLIAM ALEXANDER, <hi rendition="#italic">Alderman and Justice of
                                    the Peace</hi>.</item>
                            <item>D. HOWELL, <hi rendition="#italic">Treasurer of St. John’s,
                                    Cardiff</hi>.</item>
                            <item>SAMUEL NASH.</item>
                            <item>SYDNEY D. JENKINS.</item>
                            <item>THOS. HODGE.</item>
                            <item>JOHN WILLIAMS.</item>
                            <item>JOSEPH ELLIOTT.</item>
                            <item>J. H. WILSON.</item>
                            <item>And some fifty others.</item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
